        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Check that all parent pointers in the specified subtree are correct.</para><para>This function does a traversal of the tree starting at the specified root and checks that each child points to the correct parent. If not, then an error message is printed and the function returns false. If you do not want error messages, then pass a closed output stream.</para><para>Safety: This function is not thread safe. </para>        </detaileddescription>
